      "message": "This also changes comment porting for merges. `CommentPorter.loadCommitMappings` uses `listModifiedFiles(PS_A, PS_B)` without `skipRebaseFiltering`, and `GitPositionTransformer` treats files missing from the mappings as unchanged. On a merge you can comment on files that aren\u0027t in `PS vs Parent 1` (e.g. while viewing against Parent 2). If P1_A -\u003e P1_B changed such a file, the comment now stays on the old line, or on a file that was deleted. Before, merges were always \"related\", so all files were in the mappings. Should `CommentPorter` pass `skipRebaseFiltering(true)`?",
